    "timing": "System.nanoTime around actual JDBC execute and commit. For each locked row, acquisition is within SELECT FOR UPDATE start/end and release within commit start/end. Report conservative hold brackets [commitStart-selectEnd, commitEnd-selectStart], not exact server-side row lock timestamps. Connection/transaction setup excluded from brackets, included in chunk duration.",
    "natural_http": "Exactly two real POST /api/orders per job, launched asynchronously after order lock SELECT returns in first/last chunk, aimed at distinct first/last candidate listings. No forced pause. Capture the actual HTTP existence-check SQL interval relative to the relevant expiry commit. Retry rejections after job completion.",
    "controlled_probes": "Hold after actual listing UPDATE and before commit; assert same-listing HTTP 400 completes while locks remain held, other-listing HTTP 201, and post-commit same-listing retry 201. Artificial duration excluded from performance results.",
    "scope": "Local temporary MySQL, no payment call, no scheduled one-minute wait, no throughput or production latency guarantee. Candidate lookup and real proxied service match scheduler; test loop varies batch size, no fallback expected."
